{#
insight/_report_dialog.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
"This mail should have produced an insight." The consent moment for a feature
that copies a mail into a table an administrator can export.

The disclosure paragraph is the reason this is a dialog at all. Reporting could
have been one click in the overflow menu — the note is optional and the server
needs nothing else — and it is not, because there is no honest way to hand
somebody's mail to their administration behind a menu entry that says only
"Report". So the sentence sits above the field, at full body size and in the
body's own colour, rather than as fine print under the buttons: it is what the
button does, not a footnote to it. InsightReport's class doc says the same
thing from the other end.

Hand-written and wrapped in the modal frame directly rather than going through
_partials/_modal_form.html.twig, for the reason calendar/_ics_subscribe gives:
that shell needs a FormView, and there is no form type behind one optional
textarea posted as JSON.

Not a <form>. The endpoint answers JSON so that the reading pane behind the
dialog is left exactly as it was — the same argument InsightActionsController
makes for dismissal — and a form submission would want a frame to navigate.

Variables:
  message  Message being reported
  report   InsightReport|null — what this person already filed about this mail.
           Present means the dialog is a correction: it says so, and the field
           opens holding the note as it stands rather than blank, which would
           read as though the old one had been thrown away.
#}
{% extends '_layout/app.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
<turbo-frame id="modal">
    <template data-ui--modal-frame-title>{{ 'insights.report.heading'|trans }}</template>

    <div data-controller="insight--report"
         data-insight--report-url-value="{{ path('app_insight_report_submit', { id: message.id }) }}"
         data-insight--report-token-value="{{ csrf_token('insight-report') }}"
         class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col">

        <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 px-6 pb-6 space-y-4 overflow-y-auto">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
                {{ 'insights.report.disclosure'|trans }}
            </p>

            {% if report is not null %}
                <p class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-success" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'insights.report.already_reported'|trans }}
                </p>
            {% endif %}

            <div class="space-y-1.5">
                <label for="insight-report-note" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">
                    {{ 'insights.report.note_label'|trans }}
                </label>
                {# maxlength is the same number the endpoint truncates to, so
                   the field cannot promise to keep more than the column does.
                   The server still cuts: a maxlength is a statement to a
                   browser, not a guarantee to a database. #}
                <textarea id="insight-report-note"
                          data-insight--report-target="note"
                          rows="3"
                          maxlength="{{ constant('App\\Entity\\Insight\\InsightReport::MAX_NOTE_CHARS') }}"
                          autofocus
                          placeholder="{{ 'insights.report.note_placeholder'|trans }}"
                          class="w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                                 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">{{ report ? report.note : '' }}</textarea>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2 px-6 pb-6 pt-3 shrink-0">
            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->ui--modal#close"
                    class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-8 px-3.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                           text-ink-soft bg-field border border-field hover:bg-hover
                           focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                           transition-colors duration-100">{{ 'insights.report.cancel'|trans }}</button>

            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->insight--report#submit"
                    class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-8 px-3.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-accent-ink
                           bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong active:bg-blue-800
                           focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                           transition-colors duration-100">{{ 'insights.report.submit'|trans }}</button>
        </div>

        {# The confirmations, rendered here and cloned by the controller rather
           than assembled in JavaScript: a toast built by hand in a controller
           is a second copy of _partials/_toast.html.twig that drifts from it —
           mail/sync_now_controller carries one, and it is already a theme
           behind. Cloned BEFORE the dialog closes, so it does not matter that
           closing empties the frame.

           Two of them, because a report and a correction are different news:
           "we have it" reads as a lie to somebody who reported this mail last
           week and has just added a sentence to what they said then. #}
        <template data-insight--report-target="successToast">
            {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
                message: 'insights.report.success'|trans,
                type: 'success',
            } only %}
        </template>

        <template data-insight--report-target="alreadyToast">
            {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
                message: 'insights.report.already_reported'|trans,
                type: 'info',
            } only %}
        </template>
    </div>
</turbo-frame>
{% endblock %}
